<title>GERMANY: VEW sees rise in 1997 earnings.</title>
<headline>VEW sees rise in 1997 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>DORTMUND, Germany 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electricity utility VEW AG said on Monday it expected its 1997 earnings to increase after group net profit rose 8.5 percent to 109 million marks in the first six months.</p>
<p>The company said in its interim report its forecast was based on the expectation of cost reductions this year. First-half sales fell 0.6 percent to 4.32 billion marks.</p>
<p>In 1996, VEW's net profit rose 12.5 percent to 281 million marks on sales of 8.59 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
